# Test-only key fixtures are intentionally committed (see crates/wheel-api/tests/support.rs); they
# sign nothing real and guard nothing. Everything else key-shaped stays out.
#
# The exception is per-directory rather than per-file: naming each fixture individually is a list
# somebody has to remember to extend, and forgetting is silent locally — the file exists on the
# machine that made it, so only CI ever sees the `include_str!` fail. That is exactly how the
# Ed25519 fixture reached a green local build and a red CI.
*.pem
!crates/wheel-api/tests/fixtures/*.pem

# PM hand-off copies, not part of the tree
/external.rs
/host-fmt-plus-wip.patch
qa/e2e/node_modules/
qa/e2e/test-results/
qa/e2e/playwright-report/
qa/e2e/node_modules/
qa/e2e/playwright-report/
qa/e2e/test-results/
target-cov

# Run artifacts: engine logs kept from a failed suite. Evidence for the run that
# produced them, meaningless to anyone else, and stale the moment it is committed.
qa/artifacts/

# Coverage instrumentation drops these beside the crate that produced them.
*.profraw
